  "result": "Internal Error ()\nciteturn28view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn27view3\",\"id\":22}); \nFailed to fetch https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/compounds/16493/: (502) Bad Gateway--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSource: Carini p et al, 2014 (https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/sources/151/)\nciteturn28view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 10 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn27view3\",\"id\":30}); Total lines: 28\nL0: MediaDB\nL1: \nL2: Username:  Password:\nL3: \nL4: Site Navigation:\nL5:   * 【0†Home Page】\nL6:   * 【1†Compounds】\nL7:   * 【2†Media Formulations】\nL8:   * 【3†Organisms】\nL9:   * 【4†Sources】\nL10:   * 【5†Biomass Compositions】\nL11:   * 【6†Downloads】\nL12:   * 【7†Growth Data】\nL13: \nL14:   * First author: Carini P\nL15:   * Journal: Nature Communications\nL16:   * Year: 2014\nL17:   * Title: Methane production by phosphate-starved SAR11 chemoheterotrophic marine bacteria.\nL18:   * Link to 【8†Article†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL19:   * Link to 【8†Pubmed†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL20: Associated Growth Data:\nL21:   1. 【9†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + 2-aminoethylphosphonic acid】\nL22:   2. 【10†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + glucose 6-phosphate】\nL23:   3. 【11†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + methylphosphonic acid】\nL24:   4. 【12†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + phosphite】\nL25:   5. 【13†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + phosphoserine】\nL26:   6. 【14†Pelagibacter sp HTCC7211 on Ams1 (pyruvate+glycine) + thiamin + ribose 5-phosphate】\nL27: © 2014, Institute for Systems Biology, All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHutner's Trace Elements - Chlamydomonas Resource Center (https://www.chlamycollection.org/hutners-trace-elements/ ; rewritten summary of https://www.chlamycollection.org/methods/media-recipes/hutners-trace-elements/)\nciteturn28view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn27view2\",\"id\":15}); Redirected to URL: https://www.chlamycollection.org/methods/media-recipes/hutners-trace-elements/; Total lines: 134\nL0:   * 【0†Pricing & Shipping】\nL1:   * 【1†Depositing Strains】\nL2:   * 【2†Manual Payment】\nL3:   * 【3†Contact Us】\nL4: \nL5:   * Search:\nL6:   * 【4†Strains】\nL7:   * 【5†Plasmids】\nL8:   * 【6†Full Site】\nL9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: Keyword [Input]\nL13: \nL14: Chromosome [Select]\nL15: \nL16: Locus [Input]\nL17: \nL18: Source [Select]\nL19: \nL20: Accession Year [Select]\nL21: \nL22: Collection [Select]\nL23: \nL24: Search\nL25: \nL26: [Button: Reset]\nL27: \nL28: [Input]\nL29: \nL30: Keyword [Input]\nL31: \nL32: Source [Select]\nL33: \nL34: Accession Year [Select]\nL35: \nL36: Search\nL37: \nL38: [Button: Reset]\nL39: \nL40: [Input]\nL41: \nL42: Keyword [Input]\nL43: \nL44: Search\nL45: \nL46: View all:\nL47:   * 【7†Strains】\nL48:   * 【8†Plasmids】\nL49:   * 【9†BACs】\nL50:   * 【10†Fosmids】\nL51:   * 【11†Educational Kits】\nL52:   * 【12†Mapping Kits】\nL53:   * 【13†cDNA Libraries】\nL54:   * 【14†Media】\nL55: # Hutner’s Trace Elements\nL56: ### Hutner’s Trace Elements\nL57: \nL58: from Hutner et al., Proc. Am. Philos. Soc. 94: 152-170 (1950)\nL59: \nL60: \nL61: \nL62: For 1 liter final mix, dissolve each compound in the volume of water indicated.  The EDTA should be dissolved in boiling water, and the FeSO4 should be prepared last to avoid oxidation.\nL63: \nL64: EDTA disodium salt               50 g                250 ml H_{2}O\nL65: \nL66: ZnSO4. 7 H2O                         22 g               100 ml\nL67: \nL68: H3BO3                                     11.4 g             200 ml\nL69: MnCl2. 4 H2O                          5.06 g             50 ml\nL70: \nL71: CoCl2. 6 H2O                          1.61 g              50 ml\nL72: \nL73: CuSO4.5H2O                           1.57 g              50 ml\nL74: \nL75: (NH4)6Mo7O24. 4 H2O         1.10 g              50 ml\nL76: \nL77: FeSO4. 7 H20                          4.99 g              50 ml\nL78: \nL79: Mix all solutions except EDTA.  Bring to boil, then add EDTA solution.  The mixture should turn green.  When everything is dissolved, cool to 70 degrees C.\nL80: Keeping temperature at 70, add 85 ml hot KOH (20%).\nL81: \nL82: Cool to room temperature and bring to 1 liter final volume.\nL83: \nL84: Usually the solution will be clear green initially but will turn dark red or purple over the next few days and leave a rust-brown precipitate.  If no precipitate forms, or the solution remains green, check the pH.  It should be about 6.7.  If it’s radically off this, try adding either KOH or HCl to adjust it.\nL85: The ritual calls for stoppering the flask with a cotton plug (to allow air exchange) and swirling it once a day for 1 to 2 weeks. Or better yet, use a 5 or 10 ml pipette (with a cotton filter at the top) pushed through a foam plug and bubble air through the solution for one week.\nL86: \nL87: Filter through two layers of Whatman #1 filter paper; repeat if necessary until the solution is clear.\nL88: If the planets are correctly aligned and all the proper incantations have been done, the final product will approximate a good Bordeaux in color.  However, even a subtle shift in pH can cause a color change.  We had one batch that looked like grape Koolaid but worked fine.\nL89: \nL90: Store refrigerated or frozen in convenient aliquots.\nL91: \nL92: This can be made in larger batches – 2 or 3 liters – if you prefer.\nL93: \nL94: 【15†Printable PDF】\nL95: ###\nL96: ### Sulfur-free trace elements\nL97: \nL98: Adapted from Hutner et al., Proc. Am. Philos. Soc. 94: 152-170 (1950)\nL99: \nL100: \nL101: \nL102: For 1 liter final mix, dissolve each compound in the volume of water indicated.  The EDTA should be dissolved in boiling water.\nL103: \nL104: EDTA disodium salt               50 g               250 ml H_{2}O\nL105: \nL106: ZnCl2                                       10.0 g            100 ml\nL107: \nL108: H3BO3                                     11.4 g            200 ml\nL109: \nL110: MnCl2. 4 H2O                          5.06 g             50 ml\nL111: CoCl2. 6 H2O                           1.61 g             50 ml\nL112: \nL113: CuCl2. 2 H2O                           1.00 g             50 ml\nL114: \nL115: (NH4)6Mo7O24. 4 H2O          1.10 g             50 ml\nL116: \nL117: FeCl2.4 H2O                             3.60 g             50 ml\nL118: \nL119: As for the usual trace elements recipe, mix all solutions except EDTA. Bring to boil, then add EDTA solution. The mixture should turn green. When everything is dissolved, cool to 70 degrees C. Keeping temperature at 70, add 85 ml hot KOH (20%).\nL120: Bring the final solution to 1 liter total volume and aerate for 1-2 weeks.\nL121: \nL122: The color is the same as the original trace mix.\nL123: \nL124: 【15†Printable PDF】\nL125: \nL126: \nL127: \nL128: 【16†Image†dakg4cmpuclai.cloudfront.net】\nL129: ## Cart\nL130: \nL131: Total $0.00\nL132: \nL133: 【17†Go to cart page】\n"
